# Agentic Infrastructure & Deterministic Data Flows | 2026-04-06

## 🔥 Story of the Day
### [Engineering Storefronts for Agentic Commerce](https://oreillyradar.substack.com/p/engineering-storefronts-for-agentic) — O'reilly Radar - Substack
The architecture of commerce is undergoing a fundamental shift, moving away from persuasive marketing copy and subjective UI/UX towards deterministic data contracts as autonomous AI agents take over the buyer role. The technical framework proposed is the **"Sandwich Architecture,"** which mandates a three-layer pipeline: an LLM Translator to convert ambiguous human intent into rigid JSON structure, a deterministic Executor layer to enforce strict validation (e.g., Pydantic schemas), and a final LLM Judge for selection ranking.

This infrastructure change has profound implications for MLOps pipelines. When testing, the author demonstrated that product data provided as rich, narrative marketing copy caused the system to fail validation within 12 milliseconds. Conversely, a competitor providing only structured data, such as a specific `{"water_resistance_mm": 20000}`, was successfully evaluated. This forces engineering focus upstream: product data—including conditional logic, pricing, and feature matrices—must be exposed via clean, machine-readable APIs, suggesting a future "Universal Commerce Protocol" manifest.

For those building agentic systems, the critical takeaway is elevating the importance of robust, typed data contracts in the orchestration layer. The ambiguity inherent in LLMs must be strictly constrained by a reliable, deterministic execution layer to meet business logic requirements.

